                            Preamble

  The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure
cooperation with the community in the case of network server software.

  The licenses for most software are designed to take away your freedom to
share and change it.  By contrast, our General Public Licenses are intended
to guarantee your freedom to share and change all versions of the software,
to make sure the software is preserved as free software for all its
users.

  This Public License is designed specifically to ensure that, when a
user uses a software program through a computer network, with no transfer
of a copy, the licensee shall be obligated to give the source code
to the user.  This is precisely an agreement that anticipates a
social contract that will enable cooperation in the community.

  The vast majority of the software is already used without licenses, more
or less openly, this license is designed to make it a requirement that
if you use it, you must be a contributor.  If modified, you must provide
the source code of your derivatives.  If used on a network server, you
must also provide the source code.

  The final goal is to make free software available to everyone as a
contributor.

  The GNU Affero General Public License is based on the GNU General
Public License, version 3 ("GPLv3"), and is not an identical license,
though it is a close copy.  The additional terms, version 3, section 13,
specifically the "remote network interaction" requirement, apply to this
license.

